      "side": 1,
      "message": "This description is unclear. It endures sensitive threads don\u0027t block because we return early or because we guarantee some progress? Please clarify/simplify this comment.\n\nIIUC you do 2 things here:\n1. you try to avoid blocking other threads\n2. you try to guarantee some progress so that the calling thread does not retry forever (this particular check).\n\nI don\u0027t know if this `copied` check will actually guarantee progress. Consider the case when copied\u003d\u003d0, then we do mmap_read_unlock(), copy the page and then goto retry. Over there we call mmap_read_trylock() and if contention is still there we will break without any progress returning -EAGAIN. Not sure how important this guarantee is but it\u0027s definitely not guaranteed 100% here.",
